WEBVTT

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.358
Ranmaru Shidou, huh?

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.991
Taking all of the circumstances
up until now into consideration...

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.093
...there really isn't any mistaking
that he's a symbiont, too.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.128
The question is, how are they
going to react to this?

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:57.603
It seems like there was quite
a spectacular scuffle

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.043
at the crime lab.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.807
Speaking of which,
how's Shiraishi?

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.714
It's effectively being treated
like it was an accidental death.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.842
That's fine.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:08.445
So what do you think,
Inspector Ibuki?

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.580
Hmm?

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:12.887
Supposing he is a symbiont,
then what if...

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:16.327
If the time comes,
we'll deal with him.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.627
Hey, where is he today?

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.605
He's off today.
Looks like he's on vacation.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:27.833
Vacation?

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.569
The guy that wouldn't
take a break

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.133
even if he were eaten
by a monster.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:33.805
Well, it sounds like he ruined
the Chief's mood,

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.507
and said something like
he'd "beat the hell" out of him.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.311
Seriously?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.749
But I am grateful, you know.

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:42.243
This means we'll have some peace
and quiet for a few days.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.482
Yeah, really.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:46.014
Shindo... Shindo!

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.048
What?

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.493
Are you really okay?

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.996
You spaced out.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.726
Yeah, I'm perfectly fine.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.234
Hey, by the way, how did it go?

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.258
Did what go?

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.361
Don't play dumb.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.338
You know, with Rokujo
from Section Two.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.568
Jeez, I mean,
you just had a date...

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.407
...with that gorgeous woman
from the crime lab,

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.845
and now Rokujo?

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.976
Seriously, you look like
a stick-in-the-mud, but...

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.781
Don't get me wrong.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.516
I only met with Rokujo
as part of an investigation.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.080
And my date with Yukino
wasn't anything special...

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.614
You call her "Yukino"?

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.320
Hey, who's that?

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:23.386
That gorgeous woman
from the crime lab.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.829
Why you!
What kind of guy are you?

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.162
You're being noisy, guys.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.224
Oh, crap.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.929
Shindo, come with me for a bit.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.231
Y-Yes, sir.

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.499
There's something I need
to talk to you about.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.099
Kureha.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.475
Hmm?

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:42.572
I want to ask your opinion.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.412
What are you going
to do about him?

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.850
It's already been decided, right?

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:47.875
Or could it be...

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.978
We want to avoid a failure.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.649
A failure?

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.863
That's fine.
I'll go and check.

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.189
My way.

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:08.631
Damn it.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:14.210
Is it okay for you
to drink so much, Chief?

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.715
Shut up!
I'm in a bad mood today!

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.774
You drink up too, Shindo!

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.013
N-no, I'll pass.

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:23.614
I came here because Mr. Muramasa
told me to.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:26.557
Damn it, I was wondering
what was up.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.726
Shindo, this is
a special assignment.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.431
Go and spend time
with the Chief tonight.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.732
Damn it, what does he mean,
"special assignment"?

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.294
This is just me listening
to him bitch.

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:43.435
I would rather be doing
paperwork than this.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:46.809
Hey! What are you
muttering about?

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:49.337
Hey, old man!
Give him some sake, too!

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.576
Right-o!

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.675
Even though
you've become a cop,

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:53.879
you haven't changed,
have you, Kaoru?

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.945
You still care about your juniors.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:59.480
You moron!
I told you to stop talking like that!

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.390
Excuse me, sir.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:03.759
What did the Chief do
before all this?

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.128
Well, he was quite flashy on his bike,
vroom-vroom!

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.725
Stop dredging up
needless things!

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:09.792
Damn it.

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:15.464
Shindo, did you go
to the crime lab?

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:16.497
What?

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.806
What in the world happened?

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:21.245
Well, you see...

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.942
Last night, the guys
from the Security Section showed up

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.645
and demanded that I let them
speak to you.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.888
I made them go away, of course.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:33.289
They say that you had
an accident or something,

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.055
but it couldn't be you.

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:37.528
Chief, actually...

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:38.552
Huh?

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:41.555
Heya!

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:43.228
W-Why you!

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:47.638
Lieutenant... Suzuka?
Why in the world?

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:50.699
It's a nice night.
I thought that I'd go for a walk.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:51.971
On a motorcycle?

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.035
Right.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.239
How about joining me, Shindo?

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:59.683
H-Hold on a sec!
Before that, I have business with you!

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:02.051
Oh my, I'm sorry,
but I can't drink.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:03.578
They'll take away my license.

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:05.318
That ain't what I mean!

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.519
What in the world are you up to?

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:10.121
Don't pretend
you don't know anything!

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:12.188
I know that you guys have been
concealing the information

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:14.529
on those monsters
and the scattered body part murders!

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.626
We're not concealing anything.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:18.034
They're open to the public.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.435
What!?

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:21.565
The information that you guys
need, that is.

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:24.372
D-Don't mess with me!

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.378
I'm not messing with you.

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:28.209
If we were really hiding it...

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:30.511
...you wouldn't be able
to sit here right now...

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.575
...idly drinking sake, would you?

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.108
Are you threatening me?

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.381
Heavens no.

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:37.889
You'll give me a bad name.

00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:39.221
I'm not like you.

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:40.247
What did you say!?

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.419
C-Chief...

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:42.655
Hey, Shindo...

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:44.788
Isn't it boring just sitting here...

00:07:44.831 --> 00:07:46.822
...drinking with an irritating,
old former biker?

00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:48.800
What? E-err...

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.229
Come on a late night date
with me.

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:56.505
Wha...

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:00.905
Okay then, I'm going to borrow
him for a little while.

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:02.915
Hey, don't just do whatever you
want with my subordinates!

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:05.179
And since you are on vacation,

00:08:05.218 --> 00:08:06.981
be sure to do something special
for your family,

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:08.486
so little Ruru doesn't end up
hating you!

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:11.620
See ya!

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:13.522
Hey! Give him back!

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:16.221
You little thief!
You bag snatcher!

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:24.925
Umm...

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:26.996
Is this really all right?

00:08:27.039 --> 00:08:28.097
What do you mean?

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.266
The Chief!

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:31.367
Oh, everything will be
perfectly fine.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.037
Really?

00:08:33.079 --> 00:08:34.171
More importantly...

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:36.408
...don't you have something
you want to ask me?

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:38.314
What?

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:40.114
Okay then, hold on tight!

00:08:50.997 --> 00:08:52.487
Why?

00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:53.521
What?

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:56.831
Why did you bring me
to a place like this?

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.200
Who knows?

00:08:59.305 --> 00:09:01.330
Maybe because the wind
feels so nice here.

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:05.037
Lieutenant Suzuka.

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:07.739
Hmm, one more thing.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.270
What's that?

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:10.475
What you call me.

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:11.505
Huh?

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:13.519
Calling me Lieutenant Suzuka.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:16.215
It's like something
out of a cop drama, right?

00:09:16.255 --> 00:09:18.450
And that's what you would call
an old veteran, you know?

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:19.480
Right.

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.823
Isn't there anything cooler you
could call me?

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:24.227
Um... Miss Suzuka?

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:26.254
Or how about Kureha?

00:09:26.299 --> 00:09:28.392
No, big sis Suzuka.

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:30.925
That's not it.
Big sis Kureha?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:34.371
I'm pretty much
the same age as you.

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:35.396
What?

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:37.875
So I seem older to you?

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.970
Or is it that you feel like
a younger brother compared to me?

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:43.777
Well, either way.

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:45.511
You can call me Kureha.

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:48.111
Umm, by the way... Kureha...

00:09:48.154 --> 00:09:50.281
Lieutenant,
about the crime lab...

00:09:50.323 --> 00:09:51.517
Aren't you hot?

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:53.320
Y-Yeah...

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:57.057
It looks like they were able
to save her.

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:58.085
What?

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.563
Yukino.

00:09:59.599 --> 00:10:00.964
She lost a lot of blood.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.059
It looked like things were
dangerous for a while, though...

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:05.969
Really? That's good.

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:10.502
What's the matter?

00:10:10.543 --> 00:10:13.808
If there's something you want
to ask, go ahead and ask.

00:10:13.846 --> 00:10:17.976
Recently, because so many things
have been happening so quickly,

00:10:18.017 --> 00:10:19.143
I don't know what in the world...

00:10:19.185 --> 00:10:21.346
I know.

00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:23.184
Er... um...

00:10:23.222 --> 00:10:26.191
Well, why not?
We are on a date after all.

00:10:26.225 --> 00:10:27.249
Right.

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:31.724
Mmm, the wind feels nice.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:32.753
Oh!

00:10:37.536 --> 00:10:40.699
By the way, Lieutenant,
why are you in the Tokko?

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.575
Is that a secret?

00:10:47.847 --> 00:10:50.680
To be honest,
I really didn't want to.

00:10:50.716 --> 00:10:52.980
I guess you could say
it's how things ended up being.

00:10:53.019 --> 00:10:56.113
Or, well, destiny, maybe?

00:10:56.155 --> 00:10:57.383
Hey, Shindo.

00:10:57.423 --> 00:10:58.447
Yeah?

00:10:58.491 --> 00:11:00.083
How about we head over there?

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:09.528
Oh, it's so pretty!

00:11:09.568 --> 00:11:12.799
Lieutenant, please don't get
so excited.

00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:14.863
It's kind of embarrassing.

00:11:14.907 --> 00:11:16.534
Don't worry about that!

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:34.925
I figured you for a more
cool-headed person, Lieutenant.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.827
Actually, you're not quite
a person...

00:11:37.863 --> 00:11:39.524
What did you say?

00:11:39.565 --> 00:11:42.227
N-No, I mean that what you do
isn't humanly possible.

00:11:42.268 --> 00:11:43.735
Er, not that.

00:11:43.769 --> 00:11:45.327
How should I put this?

00:11:45.371 --> 00:11:47.532
Either way, what am I, a monster?

00:11:54.847 --> 00:11:57.077
Oh, big brother is so late!

00:11:57.116 --> 00:12:00.051
Where in the world is he,
and what is he doing!?

00:12:19.505 --> 00:12:23.202
It seems like we've come
to a unsavory part of town.

00:12:25.344 --> 00:12:26.641
Whoa!

00:12:26.679 --> 00:12:29.705
Lieutenant, what are you doing?

00:12:35.187 --> 00:12:37.519
Shindo, you're more innocent
than I thought.

00:12:37.556 --> 00:12:39.615
That's not the problem.

00:12:42.461 --> 00:12:43.621
You remind me of him.

00:12:43.662 --> 00:12:44.856
What?

00:12:46.799 --> 00:12:48.858
Hmm?

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:49.890
Hey.

00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:52.904
How about we run away somewhere,
just the two of us?

00:12:52.938 --> 00:12:53.927
What?

00:12:53.973 --> 00:12:56.567
No matter what happens,
we'll just leave everything behind.

00:12:59.078 --> 00:13:00.409
Just kidding!

00:13:11.657 --> 00:13:14.626
Hey, how about we start
heading back?

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.685
It's gotten pretty late,
after all.

00:13:16.729 --> 00:13:18.196
That's true.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.960
I'd bet that Saya is probably
worried, too.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.901
You've heard
from Shiraishi, right?

00:13:23.936 --> 00:13:24.925
Huh?

00:13:25.938 --> 00:13:28.065
About what's going on right now.

00:13:29.742 --> 00:13:32.210
About what you really are.

00:13:34.013 --> 00:13:38.950
At this rate, people are going
to end up being eaten by demons.

00:13:38.984 --> 00:13:41.077
That's what
Director Shiraishi said.

00:13:42.321 --> 00:13:46.155
And he called me a symbiont.

00:13:46.192 --> 00:13:47.181
Lieutenant!

00:13:47.226 --> 00:13:51.253
What's going on?
What does he mean "symbiont"?

00:13:51.297 --> 00:13:53.993
What's happening inside of me!?

00:14:13.219 --> 00:14:14.345
Umm...

00:14:14.386 --> 00:14:17.048
My younger brother, Akito,
lies here.

00:14:17.089 --> 00:14:18.386
Just like my parents.

00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:20.051
What?

00:14:20.092 --> 00:14:23.084
Shindo, I used to live
in Machida, too.

00:14:24.296 --> 00:14:25.957
In the same apartment complex
as you.

00:14:27.766 --> 00:14:30.633
My parents were also killed
by those things.

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:33.001
Just like yours.

00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:36.735
So it was...
it was their handiwork!

00:14:38.444 --> 00:14:42.005
Shindo... do you hate them?

00:14:42.047 --> 00:14:44.140
I want to kill them all.

00:14:44.183 --> 00:14:45.309
I see.

00:14:45.351 --> 00:14:47.444
Akito said the same thing.

00:14:47.486 --> 00:14:48.475
What?

00:14:49.221 --> 00:14:52.520
Back then, both my younger
brother and I were saved.

00:14:52.558 --> 00:14:55.118
So what happened
to your younger brother?

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:01.730
Kureha, up until now,
I was living for one reason...

00:15:01.767 --> 00:15:04.463
...to get revenge
on my parents' killers.

00:15:04.503 --> 00:15:07.131
Please!
Tell me what's really going on!

00:15:07.172 --> 00:15:10.767
You won't be able to go back
to how things were if you know.

00:15:10.809 --> 00:15:12.208
Are you okay with that?

00:15:15.781 --> 00:15:18.272
My younger brother
was a symbiont.

00:15:19.652 --> 00:15:20.846
Just like me.

00:15:25.224 --> 00:15:27.454
On that day, by chance,

00:15:27.493 --> 00:15:29.723
Akito and I had gone shopping
on our bike.

00:15:32.998 --> 00:15:36.092
Hey, Akito!
Aren't you going too fast?

00:15:36.135 --> 00:15:37.830
This is normal!

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.667
Jeez.

00:15:39.705 --> 00:15:42.538
That's why I was against you
getting your license.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.777
What's that?

00:15:45.811 --> 00:15:46.800
Hmm?

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.240
We knew right away
that something was wrong.

00:15:54.386 --> 00:15:58.823
We hurried back to our parents'
apartment, number 304, but...

00:16:01.593 --> 00:16:03.561
Father...

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:04.823
Mother...

00:16:05.965 --> 00:16:09.594
Who... who did this!?

00:16:10.602 --> 00:16:12.297
Akito, wait!

00:16:21.613 --> 00:16:22.773
Akito!

00:16:27.619 --> 00:16:29.143
- Big sis!
- Akito!

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:49.698
When I came to,
I was in a hospital bed.

00:16:49.742 --> 00:16:54.475
And afterwards,
whether we wanted to or not,

00:16:54.513 --> 00:16:58.279
we learned
that it wasn't just a dream.

00:16:59.651 --> 00:17:01.175
Who are you?

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:05.179
There's no need to worry.
I'm your friend.

00:17:05.958 --> 00:17:08.188
You've been asleep
for two years now.

00:17:08.227 --> 00:17:10.161
- What?
- What?

00:17:13.232 --> 00:17:14.221
What are you doing?

00:17:14.266 --> 00:17:17.895
It's all right.
Nothing to worry about.

00:17:24.576 --> 00:17:27.136
Show me yours, too.

00:17:27.179 --> 00:17:28.373
S-Stay away!

00:17:30.215 --> 00:17:33.013
Please, I have to confirm it.

00:17:33.052 --> 00:17:34.041
No!

00:17:34.086 --> 00:17:35.610
Don't you hate them?

00:17:36.655 --> 00:17:37.644
Them?

00:17:37.689 --> 00:17:40.715
Yes, I'm talking about the ones...

00:17:40.759 --> 00:17:42.283
...that mercilessly murdered
your parents...

00:17:42.327 --> 00:17:43.919
...and all of the people
in the apartment complex.

00:17:43.962 --> 00:17:45.657
Don't you want revenge?

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.428
Can we get revenge?

00:17:51.336 --> 00:17:52.928
You two can.

00:18:06.552 --> 00:18:11.080
Ryouko was searching for other
survivors from Machida, like us.

00:18:11.123 --> 00:18:14.991
People with a tattoo
somewhere on their bodies.

00:18:17.362 --> 00:18:20.991
To put it into words,
this pattern is a mark.

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:24.469
It shows that they exist
inside you.

00:18:24.503 --> 00:18:26.596
Exist inside?

00:18:26.638 --> 00:18:28.105
They do?

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:30.506
Right. Inside us.

00:18:30.542 --> 00:18:32.635
That's why we're symbionts.

00:18:32.678 --> 00:18:36.580
At the same time, it's also
the only power that can defeat them.

00:18:38.217 --> 00:18:42.210
Shindo, you have a mark
like this too, right?

00:18:44.056 --> 00:18:46.490
You don't have to hide it.

00:18:46.525 --> 00:18:48.186
I already know about it.

00:18:49.761 --> 00:18:52.730
By the way, do you know
the story of the Box of Druj?

00:18:52.764 --> 00:18:56.393
Well, Director Shiraishi had
mentioned something about that.

00:18:56.435 --> 00:18:58.300
Shiraishi, huh?

00:18:58.337 --> 00:19:00.635
That poor man.

00:19:00.672 --> 00:19:02.435
But he got what he deserved.

00:19:02.474 --> 00:19:05.375
The Director mentioned
a demon's gate...

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.810
...and 108 parts or something.

00:19:07.846 --> 00:19:09.108
What in the world is that?

00:19:10.782 --> 00:19:12.545
That legend is the truth.

00:19:12.584 --> 00:19:13.573
Eh?

00:19:13.619 --> 00:19:16.611
Someone gathered
the 108 parts,

00:19:16.655 --> 00:19:20.751
put the box together,
and opened the gate.

00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:23.556
And then the gate became
a gigantic hole...

00:19:23.595 --> 00:19:25.085
...and began
summoning them.

00:19:27.933 --> 00:19:31.027
Then for some reason...

00:19:31.069 --> 00:19:33.469
...one group of them, in other words,
the phantoms...

00:19:33.505 --> 00:19:35.871
...started entering us.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.113
Shindo...

00:19:43.148 --> 00:19:46.811
...the Tokko's mission is to gather
those 108 parts,

00:19:46.852 --> 00:19:50.583
put that 'box' together
one more time, and close the gate.

00:19:50.622 --> 00:19:54.456
In other words,
completely close off their exit.

00:19:54.493 --> 00:19:58.190
But where in the world
are those parts?

00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.492
Inside of them.

00:19:59.531 --> 00:20:00.520
Inside?

00:20:00.566 --> 00:20:01.794
Right.

00:20:01.833 --> 00:20:05.667
The more of them we can kill,
the more parts we can collect.

00:20:05.704 --> 00:20:08.298
Then the ones that we've seen up
until now are also...

00:20:10.108 --> 00:20:11.803
Those are just peons.

00:20:11.843 --> 00:20:13.811
The parts only exist
in the main bodies.

00:20:13.845 --> 00:20:14.937
The main bodies.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.278
What you ran into
at the crime lab.

00:20:21.053 --> 00:20:25.513
And because he's the twelfth phantom
we've dealt with up until now,

00:20:25.557 --> 00:20:27.855
we call him Number Twelve.

00:20:27.893 --> 00:20:30.225
Lieutenant... Kureha.

00:20:30.262 --> 00:20:32.822
So what are you saying
I should do?

00:20:32.864 --> 00:20:34.889
You don't need to use
"Lieutenant".

00:20:34.933 --> 00:20:37.128
Well, now that you know
the truth,

00:20:37.169 --> 00:20:39.433
I think your only choice
is to move forward.

00:20:39.471 --> 00:20:42.406
But I'll leave the final decision
up to you.

00:20:42.441 --> 00:20:44.409
Of whether you awaken it or not.

00:20:44.443 --> 00:20:46.001
Awaken?

00:20:46.044 --> 00:20:50.208
Symbionts are nothing more
than the vessels in which they exist.

00:20:50.249 --> 00:20:52.911
In order to obtain the power
to kill them,

00:20:52.951 --> 00:20:55.920
you have to awaken the phantom
that exists inside of you.

00:20:55.954 --> 00:20:58.047
There's a risk attached to it,
of course.

00:20:58.090 --> 00:20:59.785
A risk?

00:20:59.825 --> 00:21:02.089
If the phantom inside of you
is awakened,

00:21:02.127 --> 00:21:04.823
there's no guarantee that your
consciousness will remain as it is.

00:21:04.863 --> 00:21:09.061
Lf... I get taken over...

00:21:09.101 --> 00:21:11.729
Then we'll have no choice.

00:21:20.712 --> 00:21:22.339
Kureha.

00:21:22.381 --> 00:21:23.746
Yes?

00:21:23.782 --> 00:21:28.310
Um... how did
your younger brother die?

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:32.987
I killed him.

00:21:33.025 --> 00:21:34.014
What?

00:21:34.059 --> 00:21:36.619
Just kidding.
That was a joke.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.755
Shindo.

00:21:40.799 --> 00:21:41.993
Hmm?

00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:47.571
Okay, then, how about
we head back?

00:22:00.852 --> 00:22:01.841
Akito.

00:22:07.926 --> 00:22:10.394
Why... why!?

00:22:24.643 --> 00:22:26.110
Akito.

00:22:40.592 --> 00:22:45.359
Sono te wo tsunaidari

00:22:45.397 --> 00:22:50.334
Kuchizuke attari

00:22:50.369 --> 00:22:55.136
Ato sukoshi de sotto

